# {{.ProjectName}}

Kimi Code plugin scaffold generated by [plugin-kit-ai](https://github.com/777genius/plugin-kit-ai) `init`.

This lane models the observed Kimi packaged plugin bundle for portable skills and inline MCP.

## Status

- Target lane: `kimi`
- Platform family: `ide_plugin`
- Launcher: not used
- Runtime claim: packaging-only plugin lane

## First Run

```bash
plugin-kit-ai generate .
plugin-kit-ai generate --check .
plugin-kit-ai validate . --platform kimi --strict
```

Kimi Code has no non-interactive plugin CLI. The installer copies the package into `~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed` and records `plugins/installed.json`; reload Kimi or run `/plugins reload`.

## Target Files

- `plugin/plugin.yaml`: canonical shared plugin metadata and target list
- `plugin/skills/`: canonical portable skill authored source; `plugin-kit-ai init --extras` pre-seeds a starter and generate mirrors it into plugin-root `skills/`
- `plugin/mcp/servers.yaml`: canonical portable MCP authored source; `plugin-kit-ai init --extras` pre-seeds a starter and generate inlines it into `.kimi-plugin/plugin.json#mcpServers`
- root `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`: boundary docs that tell humans and agents to edit only `plugin/`
- `.kimi-plugin/plugin.json`: generated managed Kimi plugin manifest; Kimi also accepts `kimi.plugin.json`, and that file wins when both exist
- `skills/`: generated managed portable skills

## Current Boundary

- Supported in phase 1: portable `plugin/skills/**`, portable `plugin/mcp/servers.yaml`, and generated `.kimi-plugin/plugin.json`
- Kimi requires MCP servers inline in the plugin manifest. External MCP file refs are invalid on this target
- Not yet modeled in this packaged lane: first-class authored Kimi `commands`, `hooks`, `agents`, or `systemPrompt`
